---
import DefaultLayout from '@layouts/DefaultLayout.astro'
import PageHeader from '@components/PageHeader.astro'
import { Heading, Link, Avatar, AvatarGroup } from 'accessible-astro-components'
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components'
---

<DefaultLayout title="About">
  <PageHeader title="About" subtitle="Learn more about the Northfield Festival of Music & Speech" bgType="gradient" />
  <section class="my-16">
    <div class="container">
      <Heading level="h2">History of the Festival</Heading>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-32">
      <div class="space-content">
        <p>
          The Northfield Festival of Music and Speech is an annual competitive arts event held in Birmingham, England,
          focused on educating and fostering the talents of children and young people.
        </p>
        <Heading level="h3">Key Milestones & History</Heading>
        <p class="text-lg">
          <ul>
            <li>
              Establishment & Charity Status: The festival's governing constitution was formally adopted on June 14,
              1990 (with subsequent amendments in 1991 and 2003), and it was registered as a UK charity (No. 1003470) on
              July 19, 1991.
            </li>
            <li>
              Mission: Founded to promote public and youth education in the arts, the festival gives participants the
              chance to perform live before audiences, receive constructive feedback from professional adjudicators, and
              gain confidence.
            </li>
            <li>
              Format & Venue: The event features diverse classes spanning music (strings, vocal, piano) and speech and
              drama. Over recent years, it has been hosted annually at venues such as Bishop Challoner Catholic College
              in Birmingham.
            </li>
            <li>
              Affiliation: It is a member festival connected with the broader performance arts network via the <Link
                href="https://www.federationoffestivals.org.uk/festivals/615"
                isExternal>British and International Federation of Festivals (BIFF)</Link
              >.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </p>
        <Heading level="h3">Get Involved</Heading>
        <p class="text-lg">
          Our Festival can only continue to thrive with the support of volunteers and Friends. Our Festival can only
          continue to thrive with the support of volunteers and Friends. If you would like to volunteer to help on the
          Festival day, please email info@northfieldfestival.org.uk for more information.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you would like to support the Festival by becoming a Friend, please complete the form here. <Link
            href="https://forms.gle/Qod4YgdQoyQhUeat7"
            isExternal>here</Link
          >.
        </p>
        <Heading level="h3">Security</Heading>
        <p>The committee cannot be held responsible for loss of personal effects during the Festival.</p>

        <Heading level="h3">Additional Needs</Heading>
        <p>Please contact us at <Link
            href="mailto:info@northfieldfestival.org.uk">info@northfieldfestival.org.uk</Link> with any information about support a performer may require.</p>

        <Heading level="h3">Admission</Heading>
        <p>There is an entrance fee of £5 for non-performers. (Children Free). <br />Programmes on the door: £3.00.</p>

        <Heading level="h3">Venue</Heading>
        <p><Link href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/PL3nDLWTvS4nhibc7" isExternal>Bishop Challoner Catholic College, Institute Road, Kings Heath, B14 7EG</Link></p>
      

        <Heading level="h3">Officers &amp; Officials</Heading>
        <p><strong>President</strong>:<br />Philip Dukes F.G.S.M., A.R.A.M.</p>
        <p><strong>Hon. Vice President</strong>:<br />Mrs Doreen Baggett</p>
        <Heading level="h4">Friends of Northfield Festival</Heading>
